  "narration": [
    {
      "t": 0.5,
      "text": "This lane holds too many pieces per batch. Fixing that is two steps, not one."
    },
    {
      "t": 6.41,
      "text": "The lane is prepared and set to take four pieces at a time. We want two."
    },
    {
      "t": 11.68,
      "text": "So we edit that one field in the description."
    },
    {
      "t": 16.8,
      "text": "Two it is."
    },
    {
      "t": 22.8,
      "text": "But look at the last line now. kiln is still holding what it read before our edit."
    },
    {
      "t": 28.8,
      "text": "And it will not fire like that. One line, no advice."
    },
    {
      "t": 34.8,
      "text": "So prepare the lane again, which is what picks the edit up."
    },
    {
      "t": 40.8,
      "text": "Now it fires, and it tells us the batch it made and where the artifact went."
    },
    {
      "t": 46.8,
      "text": "And here is which pieces it actually took. Worth checking, because it is not the half you might assume."
    },
    {
      "t": 53.37,
      "text": "Change the description, prepare the lane again, then fire. In that order."
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Teaches the hold-count field, that a changed description leaves the lane stale until it is prepared again, and that a batch keeps the last pieces in name order."
}
